        !! ch5 exercise 'cycles':
        !!
        !! 1. guesstimations 
        !! 2. other "hands dirty"/"having fun":
        !!    - see the pythagorean identity
        !!    - illustrate powers of secant
        !!    - recognizing four graphs
        !!    - recognize 0.2 radians
        !! 3. expression Acos(Bt+C)+D or Asin(Bt+C)+D & sinusoid concept:
        !!    - from algegra to phyical description
        !!    - effect of constants on graph
        !!    - function box compositions in the abstract
        !! 4. pure geometry
        !!    - conch spiral
        !!    - top / side blueprint
        !!    - spherical coordinates 1 & 2
        !!    - door-opening angle (uses arctan)
        !! 5. delving into four graphs via algebra, geometry, & sum formulas:
        !!    - the geometric interpretation of cosx+sinx and maximizing cosx+sinx
        !!    - the geometric interpretation of cosx+sinx and rewriting as sqrt(2)cos(x-eta/2) and proof via sum formulas
        !!    - "is cos^2(theta) more closely related to cos(2theta)" etc (proof via sum formulas)
        !!    - maximization of sinx.cosx via isosets
        !!    - algebraic proof that sinx.cos <= 1/2 (easier) and that cosx+sinx <= sqrt(2) (harder)
        !! 6. 'constant ratio' geometry
        !!    - gas tank sphere
        !!    - loxodromic boat 
        !! 7. Archimedean sphere
        !!    - area-preserving property of the Lambert projection [ROTATING CENTRAL ANGLE upstream of this]
        !!    - sphere slices
        !!    - area of sphere
        !!    - volume of sphere
        !! 8. complementary angles & secant
        !!    - complement angle computation 1
        !!    - complement angle computation 2 (complement of complement)
        !!    - intersections of tangent w/ axes
        !!    - geometric evaluation of 1/A
        !!    - evaluating sec^2 two different ways & secondary trigonometric identities via algebra
        !!    - geometric interpretation of tan & cot on the unit circle
        !! 9. long division nuttiness & final numerical estimates for eta (after gas tank)
        !! 10. other:
        !!    - eta & 4eta as ratios
        !!    - rewriting Acosx + Bsinx as a sinusoid
        !!    - sum formulas for tan & cot

    |> In
        content=selection
        chapter=>>chain

